  "status_text": "A trip that zigzags between two lanes can be straightened to one lane change at most between junctions. Along each stretch you can stay in either lane at every step. At a junction, every allowed entrance connects to every allowed exit. Fix the lane where the trip starts and where it ends. Lean checked that the whole route is possible exactly when each stretch can join its allowed ends by staying put or changing lanes once. Even back-to-back junctions work if their exit and entrance lanes overlap (L-lib-397).",
